 for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and designated  L breast mass   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x4 0cm oriented fragment of breast  The superior aspect is inked black  the inferior aspect inked blue  and the posterior surface overinked orange  Much of the parenchyma is replaced by an ill defined  white  firm  stellate lesion which spans approximately 6 0cm in length  and REMOVED_DATE to 5 0cm in diameter  The lesion is partially cystic  and notable for multiple small 0 1cm soft yellow foci  The tumor margins blend in with surrounding firm and focally cystic parenchyma  The lesion grossly abuts the inferior and posterior medial margins  and is within 0 1cm of the superior  anterior and lateral margins  In the inf