hey have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and   breast cancer    skin invasion   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm skin ellipse on the surface and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary extension  The center of the skin surface contains a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm dimpling  Underneath this dimpling is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm tan firm mass that extends to the skin surface  The mass is 4 0cm from the deep resection margin  4 5cm from the inferior resection margin  10 0cm from the superior resection margin  8 0cm from the medial resection margin  and 15 0cm from lateral resection margin  The specimen has been entirely inked black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal fibrofatty breast tissue with no other focal lesions identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODES  A  medial margin  en face  B  lateral margin  en face  C  superior margin  en face  D  inferior margin  en face  E  posterior margin F H  sections of mass including skin surface  I  representative section of uninvolved breast  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary extension  ranging from 0 8cm to 2 0cm in greatest dimension  Lymph nodes are submitted as follows  J K  one large lymph node  L O 01 02  one lymph node per cassette   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   lymph node  Resident  LYNN CORNELL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin Hughes MD PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 52 CLINICAL DATA  History of endometrial carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  80   REMOVED_DATE CM  DISPLAYING ENDOCRINE CHARACTERISTICS  AND EXTENDING TO ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN AT THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPE  20   EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 24                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm breast biopsy specimen with localizing wire in place and an accompanying x ray demonstrating an ill defined mass  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 1cm firm  gray  stellate  gritty lesion  approaching 0 3cm from the nearest inked margin  The lesion is entirely submitted in cassettes A through C  the remainder in D through I  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT   BIOPSY  SMALL LESION  HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA IS PRESENT  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Najmosama Nikrui  M D  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  Mark Atkinson Vangorder  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
