Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 45 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  WITH NEURAL AND POSSIBLE VASCULAR INVASION     DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5       FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  SEE NOTE   NOTE  infiltrating carcinoma extends to inked margins and the single focus of ductal carcinoma in situ extends to within less than 0 1cm of an inked resection margin  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 18                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 03     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   9   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fibrofatty piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a well circumscribed  rubbery  tan to yellow nodule abutting all inked surfaces  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  A section was taken for BRDU studies  The remainder of the specimen is submitted entirely in A and B  Resident  Lisa H  Lerner  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING AND IN SITU CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
