sterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 94 at 07 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 6cm in greatest dimension  ill defined  tan white  gritty and firm area that grossly abuts an inked resection margin  The remainder of the specimen is predominantly composed of unremarkable breast and adipose tissue  A representative section of the lesion is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Representative sections of remainder of the specimen submitted in cassettes A through J  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
