Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 24 CLINICAL DATA  Palpable nodules at 3 o clock on the right  calcium at 12 o clock on the right      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  AMENDED CLINICAL HISTORY Revised by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Revised on 10 AUG 98 at 11 47                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  TISSUE CALCIFICATIONS    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  TWO SEPARATE FOCI SPANNING REMOVED_DATE AND REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY PRESENT AT INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA WITH CALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  Invasion of lymphatic vessels and blood vessels is not seen  BREAST  RIGHT  BREAST NODULE    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FOCALLY PRESENT AT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE CLOSEST RESECTION MARGIN  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Edited by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 16 10 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   Tissue calcifications    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast tissue calcification  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm unoriented fibroadipose breast tissue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal fibrous breast parenchyma  submitted entirely in A through F  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast nodule  is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 6cm fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Submitted entirely in G and H  Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST NODULE   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  ZUOQIN TANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  TISSUE CALCIFICATIONS    EXCISIONAL PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  BREAST NODULE    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
