he 0 4cm metastatic deposit is present in a 1 6cm lymph node  No extranodal extension is identified  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 18 20                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block F   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 14 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast solid mass at 12 o clock   4 o clock calcifications 2 wires  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm lumpectomy specimen with two needle localization wires  with the lateral wire representing calcifications and the more medial wire denoting a mass  The specimen is inked black  posterior overinked in blue  superior overinked in red  and inferior overinked in orange  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 0 5cm cystic area in the lateral portion of the breast  coming to 0 2cm from the superior resection margin  and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm firm hard white gritty mass present in the middle of the specimen coming to  0 1cm from the inferior posterior resection margin  Representative sections from lateral to medial are submitted in cassettes A F  Tissue away from the mass is submitted in cassette G  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_