Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 24 CLINICAL DATA  75 year old with infitrating ductal carcinoma by biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  2  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCAL  3  EXTENSIVE SCAR FORMATION  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 21 OF 21 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  The resection margins are free of tumor  No vascular invasion is identified  Tumor is present in 5 of 18 sections  Tumor is present in biopsy site and surrounding parenchyma adjacent to biopsy site  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  05 AUG 94 at 15 11                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  Breast bloc  is a 39 x 25 x 6cm modified radical mastectomy with an overlying 30 x 18cm ellipse of skin  8cm inferior to the nipple is a healed surgical scar  The linear scar runs from lateral to medial  The scar is grossly unremarkable  0 5cm deep to the surgical scar is a 6cm in average diameter biopsy cavity lined with white  firm  fibrous tissue admixed with focal areas of circular brown tissue  Originating from the biopsy cavity is a mass of stellate white fibrous tissue which extends to 0 3cm from the inferior deep aspect  Outside on the periphery of the biopsy cavity the breast tissue consists mainly of fibroadipose tissue and is otherwise grossly unremarkable  Labeled  Axillary tail  is a 10 x 15 x 10cm mass of fibroadipose tissue consisting of firm areas of firm rubbery tissue  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected and ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1cm in average diameter  Section Code  A  biopsy cavity with skin and margin  B  biopsy cavity and deep margin  C  biopsy cavity  D  biopsy cavity  E  closest margin  deep   F  biopsy cavity  G  biopsy cavity  H  medial margin  I K  lymph nodes entirely submitted  L R  biopsy site  S T  parenchyma superior to biopsy site  U  deep margin  Resident  SCOTT O  URBAN  HMS                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  PART B  BREAST LEFT  PART C  AXILLARY NODE CONTENTS PART D  AXILLARY NODE CONTENTS   report_end  , Unchecked.
