  superior lateral nodule has a yellow white cut surface with focal areas of hemorrhage  the fibrinous biopsy cavity has a yellow white cut surface the remainder of the parenchyma has a yellow white cut surface and is grossly unremarkable  Section code  A  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity nearest to the margin at the inferior aspect of the specimen  B  Representative sections of the medial nodule  C  Representative sections of the superior lateral nodule  D  Representative section of the biopsy cavity near the superior margin  E  Representative section of the parenchyma at the superior margin  Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 11 CLINICAL DATA  Density on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 2 OF 3  EXTENDING TO A MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  ONE DUCT AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE TUMOR  ADJACENT TO A MARGIN  SLIDE D   NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The area of the positive margin was examined by the surgeon when it became apparent that the tumor was close to an edge on gross examination  an additional fragment was then excised  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN  BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 09                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm portion of breast tissue with a suture designating the area closest to the nipple  The specimen is inked black and double inked blue at the suture  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hard tan stellate mass within 0 2cm from the inked margin and 1 5cm from the suture  Note that the surgeon looked at the margins in the frozen section lab and looked at the margin  The mass is submitted in cassettes A and B  A representative section of the surrounding tissue are submitted in cassettes C   F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular portion of fibrofatty breast tissue with a suture designating the area farthest from the needle localization specimen towards nipple  The entire specimen is inked black  and the sutured area green  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no discrete lesions  The parenchyma is predominantly unremarkable adipose tissue  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes G   L  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST MASS   CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY 