erone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast biopsy left axillary node dissection   is a 21 x 7 x 2 4cm lumpectomy specimen with attached axilla  There are three guide wires in the specimen and a long stitch marking the lateral and axillary lateral margin and axillary tail  short stitch demarcating the anterior margin  and a bow tie demarcating the superior margin  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal tan yellow adipose tissue with intermixed white fibrous tissue  and numerous palpable nodules ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The nodules are ill defined and in most cases not visually discrete from the surrounding adipose and fibrous tissue  However the largest mentioned nodule is tan pink to tan white and is adjacent to a curled surgical clip  This largest nodule is 0 5cm from the anterior margin  1 5cm from the posterior margin 2 5cm from the inferior margin  2 2cm from the superior margin  and greater than 3 0cm from both the medial and lateral margins  The surgical clip is removed and representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Dominant nodule to anterior margin adjacent to curled clip  B C  Additional sections of nodule to anterior margin  D  Nodule to posterior and inferior margins  E H  Additional sections range from medial to lateral including nodular areas in all sections  I  One axillary lymph node  1 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm    quadrasected  J  One axillary lymph node  1 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm    bisected  K  One axillary lymph node  1 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm    bisected  L  One axillary lymph node  1 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5   bisected  M  Four axillary lymph nodes  0 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm    whole  N  Two axillary lymph nodes  1 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE    whole  O  Axillary cyst  1 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9   quadrasected  P Y Additional breast tissue sections  Resident  STEWART M  KNOEPP  MD   Ph D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   LYMPH NODE LEFT A , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 15 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  25     GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  75    COMEDO TYPE WITH CALCIFICATIONS  EXTENDING FAR AWAY FROM THE MASS AND TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma measures 0 9cm in greatest dimension on tissue section  and the intraductal carcinoma invades glandular tissue in about one half the sections  Blood vessel or lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD Signed On  03 AUG 93 at 16 15 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   7   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  16 AUG 93 at 09 14     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 AUG 93 at 09 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm piece of breast parenchyma with two localizing wires and an x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to show a gray pink  hard stellate lesion 0 7cm in greatest diameter  There is a 0 2cm firm  gray pink lesion at the surgical margin  A representative section of thin area is frozen as frozen section  1  Frozen section  1 will be kept frozen  The remainder of the specimen will be submitted in cassettes  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  P  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Christophe Girardet  M D                                                          