                          RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  MASS    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two parts  Labeled   1  breast tissue  mass ultrasound superior calcification  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm piece of breast  It is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hard tan well defined mass  0 4cm from nearest superior margin  frozen section  2  and 0 8cm from the nearest lateral margin  frozen section  1   3   There are firm areas in the remaining tissue but no other well defined mass  Inked as follows  lateral   green  superficial   blue  superior   b