 sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan pink lymph node which is entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 2  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm tan red left simple mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm ovoid portion of tan pink skin  There is a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unremarkable tan pink nipple  A black stitch marks the 6 o clock aspect as per requisition  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal diffuse  dense  nodular gray white fibrous tissue which comes to 0 1cm of the posterior margin in the upper outer quadrant  No discrete lesions are identified  Sectioning of the upper outer quadrant reveals several possible tan red lymph nodes up to 0 4cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from the upper outer quadrant which may represent lymph node is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm tan red right simple mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 3 1cm ovoid portion of tan pink skin  There is an eccentric REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm unremarkable tan pink nipple and a 1 3cm well healed semicircular scar along the medial aspect located 0 3cm of the medial skin margin  A black stitch designates the 12 o clock aspect as per requisition  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a poorly delineated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm gray white  stellate fibrous area in the mid to inner breast tissue  The area corresponds to the skin scar  The area comes to 1 4cm of the anterior and 2 8cm of the posterior margins  Abutting along the medial aspect of the scarred area is a somewhat well demarcated indurated gray white lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  This lesion comes to 1 7cm of the anterior and greater than 2 5cm of the posterior margin  Sectioning of the medial breast tissue reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm well circumscribed gray white fibrous nodule which comes to 1 4cm of the posterior and 1 1cm of the anterior margin The remaining mammary tissue shows diffuse dense nodular gray white fibrous tissue throughout  No other mass lesions or other gross abnormalities are identified  Sectioning of the upper outer quadrant reveals several tan red areas which may represent lymph node  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire gray white fibrous stellate scar submitted from lateral to medial with closest deep margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative uninvolved fibrous tissue lateral to scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Indurated lesion abutting medial edge of fibrous scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest deep margin to indurated lesion in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative uninvolved fibrous tissue medial to scar and lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Well defined fibrous nodule in medial breast tissue to anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from upper outer quadrant which may represent lymph node  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION  2   LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART D  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART E  CRYOSTAT FRO