d 2 0cm from the medial margin  1 8cm from the lateral margin  0 7cm from the posterior margin  1 0cm from the superior margin  0 9cm from the inferior margin  and 2 4cm from the anterior margin  There is a moderate amount of dense  gray white fibrous tissue surrounding the cavity  which focally abuts the superior and posterior margins  The remaining cut surfaces consists of yellow  lobulated adipose tissue  with interspersed gray white  focally dense fibrous tissue  which occupies approximately 25  of the cut surfaces  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity  submitted entirely  sequentially from medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Dense fibrous tissue at periphery of cavity  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative dense fibrous tissue away from biopsy site   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end  en face  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such cle