ls do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy with needle localization  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm portion of previously blue dyed fibrofatty breast tissue which has free floating localizing wire and an accompanying radiograph  There is short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral  The specimen is black inked anteriorly  blue inked posteriorly  red inked superiorly  Serially sectioning reveals REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm poorly delineated tan white gritty lesion 0 5cm from the anterior margin and comes to within 0 9cm of the superior  1 5cm of the posterior  1 0cm from the lateral  0 5cm from the inferior  2 0cm from the medial margins  The remaining parenchyma is 90  yellow lobulated fatty to 5  dense white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from lateral to medial as follows  A  lateral margin B  inferior margin C  anterior margin D  inferior margin E  mass to superior margin F  mass to anterior margin G H  mass to superior margin I J  fibrous tissue to anterior margin Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional superior superficial right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of adipose tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as K M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final shaved margin superior half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of previously blue dyed fibrofatty breast tissue which is serially sectioned  and entirely submitted as cassette N S  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final shaved margin inferior half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal a 80  previously dense white fibrous to 20  lobulated fatty tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as T Y  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  sentinel node hot and blue right breast   REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm tan rubbery fatty lymph node which is bisected to reveal a blue grey smooth surface  The specimen is entirely submitted as 2  Gross Description by  LORI MARINI Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  SMN                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Claire Bloom  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL NODE   REMOVED_CASE_ID    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  SUPERIOR HALF OF CAVITY   FINAL SHA PART E  BREAST  RIGHT  INFERIOR HALF OF CAVITY   FINAL SHA , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 45 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal mammogram  Rule out ca                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3 OF 3  PRESENT AT THE MARGIN  INCISIONAL BIOPSY   WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 05                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   1   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 56     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast tissue  with an accompanying x ray is a 3 x 2 x 1 4cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a wire not in the tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 4cm in widest diameter  firm white brown stellate lesion with ill defined borders  abutting one inked resection margin  Representative sections frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen for ERPR  A section is taken for BRDU analysis  Remainder of tissue submitted in cassettes  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  E  with the lesion in cassettes A through D  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
